Unicorn m68k mem_map failure — 2026-10-26

Environment: macOS 26.2 arm64, Python 3.12.14
Candidate venv: an alternative local digiemu venv
libunicorn.2.dylib: 806512 bytes, sha256
  a0db6bebc7506245be341971a4b7a67d012aa37ee3e46ebc39679b88137e503f

Minimal probe:
  from unicorn import Uc, UC_ARCH_M68K, UC_MODE_BIG_ENDIAN
  u = Uc(UC_ARCH_M68K, UC_MODE_BIG_ENDIAN)
  u.mem_map(0, 0x1000)

Result:
  Fatal Python error: Illegal instruction
  File ".../unicorn/unicorn_py3/unicorn.py", line 831 in mem_map
  exit status 132

The same probe fails with the 16,232,448-byte library in the decompplanner and
DT-sidecar digiemu venvs (sha256
7207c8e3d7a63118fb0bca73e01816797fd51b1d8a39a4cbc7abfd562ee59c85). No guest
instruction executes. emu.unicorn_compat therefore also exits 132 at its first
mem_map call, without producing a compatibility report.

Implication: a usable patched runtime must be built/reinstalled for this host,
or a known-good prebuilt digiemu runtime must be supplied. A different
libunicorn with a matching ABI is required before R03 can run.

Crash site from the macOS DiagnosticReports:
  exception EXC_BAD_INSTRUCTION / SIGILL
  init_cache_info -> machine_initialize -> uc_init_engine -> uc_mem_map
This is inside the emulator library's cache probing, before any guest
instruction or translation. It is therefore a host/build incompatibility of
the available libunicorn, not an R03 track-processing result. A rebuilt
patched Unicorn for this host (or a known-good prebuilt runtime) is required.
